      "sceneId": "agreeing-on-a-shared-budget",
      "kind": "stories",
      "itemId": "agreeing-on-a-shared-budget",
      "src": "/audio/stories/agreeing-on-a-shared-budget.mp3",
      "text": "Roommates Leah and Sam set a weekly budget of one hundred and twenty dollars for shared groceries and cleaning supplies. “I would rather buy less meat than cut back on fresh vegetables,” Leah says. Sam agrees, but asks, “Does that include a reserve for unexpected costs?” They allow eighty dollars for groceries and twenty-five for supplies, leaving fifteen as a buffer. “We can split the total equally, provided that personal snacks come from our own money,” Sam suggests. Leah agrees to contribute sixty dollars, but adds, “Any spending above the weekly limit needs both of us to agree first.” Sam agrees to contribute the same amount and says, “The trade-off is less variety, but we can keep our spending under control.” They will review the plan after two weeks and discuss any changes before raising the limit.",
      "textSha256": "5975f9a61a7fba2d851c974c58ed3cb5739a90b0b035c0d4ced67fdd1e8c60a3"
    },
